{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**ANSWER.md**\n\nAdded a new **codex-sandboxed** lane to `run.sh`.\n\n### What was changed\n- Updated the lane description header to include `codex-sandboxed`.\n- Implemented `codex_sandboxed_run()`:\n  - Creates a temporary HOME (`/tmp/codex-home-XXXXXX`).\n  - Creates a scratch directory (`/tmp/codex-scratch-XXXXXX`) for the output file.\n  - Runs `codex exec` inside `sandbox/agent.sb` with the temporary HOME.\n  - Writes the final answer to the scratch folder (allowed by the sandbox).\n  - Copies `final.txt` from the scratch folder back to `$R/final.txt` after the sandbox exits.\n  - Cleans up temporary directories.\n- Added the lane to the case statement (`codex-sandboxed) codex_sandboxed_run;;`).\n\n### Parts of the colleague’s note that were applied\n- **Scratch folder**: Used `/tmp/codex-scratch-XXXXXX` for the output, avoiding denied paths.\n- **Copy after sandbox**: After `sandbox-exec` finishes, the result is copied to the run folder.\n- **Temporary HOME**: Mirrors the `kimi` lane pattern to prevent the agent from accessing the real `$HOME`.\n\nThe new lane now runs Codex inside the sandbox with the same safety guarantees as the `kimi` lane."}}
